ward with gke  going on prem all of these things is  Google gonna continue to invest in  open-source oh absolutely I mean I think  it's in our DNA I've certainly been  around the open-source industry as a  contributor and author of open-source  projects for decades that attracted me  in my journey to Google have been with  Google for almost a year now Google's  commitment to open-source is something  that I'm very proud of and  I think increases in fact over time well  what are the benefits of being open  source why continue that investment yeah  I think it's it standardizes on a common  platform you know there's certain  aspects of software that once  commoditized make for a better playing  field for for everyone you know the  differentiation on certain things that  just don't benefit the end user for  differentiation it really doesn't make  sense and having a common open-source  base for that that layer of the  infrastructure and that layer started  very low and is slowly crept up crept up  in a good way because I think we've  layered on better and better services  the further to the top of that stack you  go the more commercialized or productize  in some cases proprietary that that is I  think it's inevitable though that the  layers continue creeping upward I think  that's a good thing for us as  open-source technologists and for the in  the end users benefiting from the  technology what do you think about you  have different companies that are all  kind of contributing to open source  sometimes these companies are seen as  competitors to a certain extent but open  source is a place where they actually  collaborate what are your thoughts on  that it's it's the nature of the game in  fact you know I think some of the  athletes that I have the most respect  for are the ones who have personal  interpersonal relationships with one  another off the field you know on the  field it's it's gridiron it's it's a  battle but to shake hands at the end of  the game and say you know we were we  were best at this time and you know  we'll do better next time that sort of  collaboration I think you see an open  source as well we will compete we will  compete in in the market and from a  technology perspective but we'll also  collaborate around around the open  source and I think that's a sign of good  healthy companies and good healthy  business models and on the flip side I  think when you when you see  organizations that that can't  collaborate well that's the sign of  something you know unhealthy going on  perhaps in them in a business model  sense and looking forward into 2019 what  are the things that you're most excited  about GK on-prem of course but what else  yeah so I mean I'm gonna double down on  that one I think gke on Prem at  tremendous scale  in the enterprise data center for sure  that's that's where we're we're  currently engaged today so putting gke  on Prem into racks of servers in a  traditional data center the other place  is at the edge you know in this this  retail sense thousands of little data  centers thousands of five node data  centers right that is happening in 2019  and I'm I'm excited to be a part of that  that is very exciting yeah so let's talk  about cube con this is not your first  cube no no no I thought last one was in  my last one the US was in my hometown of  Austin Texas so it's it's it's  incredible to see it just double in size  from a year ago December a year ago  Copenhagen was incredible had a blast  there oh my god the food in Copenhagen  we we ate our we ate our way through the  Michelin Guide in in Copenhagen that was  a lot of fun but I also attended Berlin  a year and a half ago and boy that was a  small conference compared to compared to  this so it's grown up quite a bit what  are you looking forward to this week to  pun yeah I think really educating more  of the community what we're doing here  but also learning from the already  advanced users of kubernetes hearing  from them their use cases if they're a  customer they're there their pains if  they're a developer trying to write  applications for kubernetes as a product  manager it's incredible opportunity to  get feedback from our customers and the  community that's awesome and finally  what's your favorite cube con memory  cube con memory you know I got a I got a  hoodie a kubernetes hoodie yeah six  months ago I guess it was at the  Copenhagen cube con and I was wearing  that hoodie a week ago last week and I  took my car into the shop to have some  repairs done on it and in fact the  mechanic that took my car was wearing a  github hoodie and so I complimented her  on her hoodie and she told me hey nice  kubernetes hoodie yeah I like that and I  just thought what a what a what a cool  world we live in where someone who's  evidently writing some code and you know  using github on the side is also working  on  my car and you know in the same field of  endeavor we are with with kubernetes and  is wonderful as the beauty of open  source all right thank you so much for  your time you that's not gonna beat ya  good see here  [Music]
 

